Subject: [PATCH] soc: imx93: preserve Linux GPIO ownership for RPMsg

The RPMsg-only M33 application does not use GPIO. Linux owns the GPIO
banks, including the touchscreen IRQ. Do not turn every pin secure-only
when remoteproc starts this firmware. Stopping M33 does not restore PCNS.

Source: MIMX9352_cm33.h, RGPIO_PCNS_NSE0: zero selects Secure access;
Non-Secure reads return zero and writes are ignored.

This patch is for the Linux-hosted RPMsg build with CONFIG_GPIO disabled.
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [application-specific resource ownership]

--- a/soc/nxp/imx/imx9/imx93/m33/soc.c
+++ b/soc/nxp/imx/imx9/imx93/m33/soc.c
@@ -57,11 +57,8 @@
 
 void soc_early_init_hook(void)
 {
-	/* Configure secure access to pin registers */
-	GPIO1->PCNS = 0x0;
-	GPIO2->PCNS = 0x0;
-	GPIO3->PCNS = 0x0;
-	GPIO4->PCNS = 0x0;
+	/* Linux owns GPIO security in this RPMsg-only build (CONFIG_GPIO=n).
+	 * Preserve PCNS: changing it breaks Linux GPIO access, including touch. */
 
 	/* keep system tick work fine during idle task */
 	GPC_CTRL_CM33->CM_MISC &= ~GPC_CPU_CTRL_CM_MISC_SLEEP_HOLD_EN_MASK;
